<!--
  Workspace Playground — CatAndMouse
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.workspace.playground.CatAndMouse
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:playground="org.blockml.bml.workspace.playground">

  <name>CatAndMouse</name>
  <type>playground:CatAndMouse</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>A playground poem about a cat and a mouse produced by a workspace transform execution</is>

  <documentation>
    Along the skirting board the small grey shadow goes,
    a whisper of feet where the lamplight barely glows.
    Above the rug the cat unfolds without a sound,
    two lanterns for eyes fixed low upon the ground.

    The mouse knows the map of every crack and seam,
    the cat knows patience, and the long slow gleam.
    A crumb is the prize, a heartbeat is the cost,
    and the kitchen holds its breath for the one who has lost.

    Then a clock strikes once and the spell breaks clean,
    the mouse is a rumour, the floor is swept and green.
    The cat sits down and washes one indifferent paw,
    as if it had never wanted the thing it never saw.
  </documentation>

  <properties>
    <title>
      <value>Along the Skirting Board</value>
    </title>
    <author>
      <value>John Doe</value>
    </author>
    <year>
      <value>2026</value>
    </year>
  </properties>

</block>
